IDENTITIES re-derived from the die map
   ok   W12 | E12 = N12 | S12 = CORE24 = 0x7777f6f6 (24 shires, 4 per column)
   ok   W12 <-> E12 is the exact mirror c -> 7-c
   ok   N12 <-> S12 is the exact mirror r -> 5-r
   ok   NULLQ12 is NULLP12 rotated 180 deg about the die centre, (r,c) -> (5-r, 7-c)
   ok   NULLP12 | NULLQ12 = CORE24, disjoint, 12 + 12
   ok   NULLP12 and NULLQ12 have the same centroid to 1e-9 mm (zero dipole)
   ok   NULLP12 and NULLQ12 are matched on all four features placements.py records
   ok   the five sweep phases are 8 shires each, mean die row exactly 2.5, mean column 1.5/2.5/3.5/4.5/5.5
   ok   every sweep phase is an exact one-column translate of the one before
   ok   the sweep's five phases union to exactly CORE24, and phase 3 IS the registered CEN8
   ok   the five orbit arms are all 4 shires x 32 = 128 harts
   ok   B4C sits exactly on the die centre
   ok   W8b/E8b are matched on n, mem_side, ns_edge, by_io and by_ms, which W12/E12 are NOT (physics.md:582 is wrong)
      (mem_side, ns_edge, by_io, by_ms):  W12 (4, 0, 0, 0)  E12 (4, 0, 2, 2)   |   W8B (3, 0, 0, 0)  E8B (3, 0, 0, 0)
